      "title": "Call to non-existent no-arg isConditionalPasskeysEnabled(): services module won't compile",
      "body": "The only definition is `protected boolean isConditionalPasskeysEnabled(UserModel user)` (UsernamePasswordForm.java:160). A grep over services/src/main/java finds no no-arg overload, so `isConditionalPasskeysEnabled()` here is a compile error.",
      "anchor": "diff"
    },
    {
      "path": "services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/authentication/authenticators/browser/UsernamePasswordForm.java",
      "line": 161,
      "severity": "blocker",
      "topic": "bug",
      "confidence": "high",
      "title": "`user != null` in the helper disables passkeys on the initial (anonymous) login page",
      "body": "Both call sites (lines 115 and 137) pass `context.getUser()` and are the only place `fillContextForm` runs for this form. The old code ran it only when the user was null (the anonymous page). With `&& user != null` the helper returns false for exactly that case. The anonymous page then gets no webauthn form data, and the passkey and conditional-UI login stops working there. That breaks the existing non-reauthentication tests, for example those that assert `//form[@id='webauth']` on the first login page. Re-authentication is supposed to be added to the anonymous case, not to replace it. The condition should be `webauthnAuth != null && webauthnAuth.isPasskeysEnabled()`. The call in UsernameForm.java:47 then needs a matching no-arg form of the check.",
      "anchor": "diff"
    },
    {
      "path": "services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/authentication/authenticators/browser/WebAuthnConditionalUIAuthenticator.java",
      "line": 65,
